# CSR profile: a site that issues from DoD PKI rather than this CA.
#
# Copy to dod-pki.env and set the values the site's registration authority actually requires
# - THESE ARE PLACEHOLDERS AND ARE NOT AUTHORITATIVE. An RA will reject a CSR whose subject
# DN does not match its policy, and the rejection typically names neither the field nor the
# expected value.
#
# Ask the RA for, and record here:
#   - the exact subject DN form, including whether CN carries an FQDN or a person/device name
#   - the required key algorithm and size
#   - whether SANs are taken from the CSR or assigned by the RA (many RAs overwrite them)
#   - the submission channel, and what comes back - a bare cert or a full chain
#
# WHEN THE CERTIFICATE COMES BACK: nothing else changes. enable-tls.sh takes a fullchain from
# any issuer and validates it against whatever is in the trust store - so put the site's roots
# in trust-anchors/ first, or the validation step will correctly refuse a perfectly good cert.
CSR_COUNTRY='US'
CSR_ORG='U.S. Government'
CSR_OU='PKI'                    # sites commonly require several OU components - ask
CSR_KEY_BITS='3072'
CSR_DIGEST='sha256'
CSR_SIGNED_BY='site registration authority - submission channel: ASK AND RECORD HERE'
